# Start existing MySQL, Redis and Garage, then run-backend.py --demo (no Fabric is needed here).
# Register a new device below, copy its id into t009.http's droneId, then create/start a NEW task.
# Set executionId/requirementId from that new task. Preserve the M2 demo tasks and seed device.
# Real passwords and the one-time deviceToken belong in an ignored REST Client environment.
# Set operatorAdminPassword in that environment; generate new boot/event/request UUIDs for a new run.
@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:8080
@executionId = REPLACE_WITH_NEW_RUNNING_EXECUTION_UUID
@requirementId = REPLACE_WITH_REQUIREMENT_UUID
@bootId = 50000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000015
@heartbeatEventId = 51000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000015
@progressEventId = 52000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000015
@clientRequestId = 53000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000015

### OrgB OPERATOR_TASK_ADMIN manages devices; ORG_ADMIN alone is insufficient
# @name adminLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username":"operator-admin","password":"{{operatorAdminPassword}}"}

### Device token is returned once; repeat registration is not token recovery
# @name device
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/drones
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.$.data.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"code":"UAV-T015-EXAMPLE"}

### Safe device list contains no deviceToken or token hash
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/drones?page=1&pageSize=20
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.$.data.accessToken}}

### After assigning this NEW device and starting its execution, report using device headers
# @name heartbeat
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/device/reports
X-Device-Id: {{device.response.body.$.data.device.id}}
X-Device-Token: {{device.response.body.$.data.deviceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"bootId":"{{bootId}}","seq":0,"eventId":"{{heartbeatEventId}}","executionId":"{{executionId}}","type":"HEARTBEAT"}

### Replay exactly: duplicate=true, original receivedAt, no new event or refreshed presence
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/device/reports
X-Device-Id: {{device.response.body.$.data.device.id}}
X-Device-Token: {{device.response.body.$.data.deviceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"bootId":"{{bootId}}","seq":0,"eventId":"{{heartbeatEventId}}","executionId":"{{executionId}}","type":"HEARTBEAT"}

### Progress is 0..100 and only grows for the execution; 100 does not complete the task
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/device/reports
X-Device-Id: {{device.response.body.$.data.device.id}}
X-Device-Token: {{device.response.body.$.data.deviceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"bootId":"{{bootId}}","seq":1,"eventId":"{{progressEventId}}","executionId":"{{executionId}}","type":"PROGRESS","progress":40}

### Device identity also owns its upload sessions, independently of user uploads
# @name upload
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/device/upload-sessions
X-Device-Id: {{device.response.body.$.data.device.id}}
X-Device-Token: {{device.response.body.$.data.deviceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"clientRequestId":"{{clientRequestId}}","requirementId":"{{requirementId}}","executionId":"{{executionId}}","filename":"inspection-sample.png","contentType":"image/png","size":79}

### Raw single part; its SHA-256 is computed by the server
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/device/upload-sessions/{{upload.response.body.$.data.uploadId}}/parts/1
X-Device-Id: {{device.response.body.$.data.device.id}}
X-Device-Token: {{device.response.body.$.data.deviceToken}}
Content-Type: application/octet-stream

< ./files/inspection-sample.png

### Durable progress is only visible to this device; another device/user cannot own this session
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/device/upload-sessions/{{upload.response.body.$.data.uploadId}}
X-Device-Id: {{device.response.body.$.data.device.id}}
X-Device-Token: {{device.response.body.$.data.deviceToken}}

### Read fresh management CAS version before disabling
# @name state
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/drones/{{device.response.body.$.data.device.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.$.data.accessToken}}

### A disabled device immediately loses report and upload access
# @name disabled
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/drones/{{device.response.body.$.data.device.id}}/enabled
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.$.data.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"enabled":false,"expectedLockVersion":{{state.response.body.$.data.lockVersion}}}

### 401 even when this is an old identical heartbeat
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/device/reports
X-Device-Id: {{device.response.body.$.data.device.id}}
X-Device-Token: {{device.response.body.$.data.deviceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"bootId":"{{bootId}}","seq":0,"eventId":"{{heartbeatEventId}}","executionId":"{{executionId}}","type":"HEARTBEAT"}

### Re-enable using the returned new version; a stale version returns 409
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/drones/{{device.response.body.$.data.device.id}}/enabled
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.$.data.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"enabled":true,"expectedLockVersion":{{disabled.response.body.$.data.lockVersion}}}

### 401: device credentials never authenticate a user endpoint
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/me
X-Device-Id: {{device.response.body.$.data.device.id}}
X-Device-Token: {{device.response.body.$.data.deviceToken}}
